00:04:45.690 --> 00:04:47.890
so we can get a really sick kid in here.

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:49.810
His renal function's decreased.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:51.190
His creatinine is elevated.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:53.240
He can't survive a transplant.

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:55.660
- According to these test
results, he most certainly can.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:57.400
The boy's mother's
already given her consent.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:58.990
- [Doogie] On your recommendation.

00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:00.820
But statistically, he's
got a better chance

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:02.290
if we just repair the valve.

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:03.474
- Basically what they're arguing about

00:05:03.474 --> 00:05:06.750
is the steps on which to take
to fix the young boy's heart.

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:09.230
The reason the young boy's
heart is in cardiac failure

00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:11.910
is because he has an impaired valve.

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:13.285
This is the value that sits in between

00:05:13.285 --> 00:05:16.520
the chambers of the heart,
the atrium and the ventricle.

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:18.580
When the heart pumps, it opens,

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:20.120
and then when the heart relaxes, it closes

00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:21.610
to make sure that the blood doesn't always

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:23.030
pool at the bottom of the heart.

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:25.240
Now if this valve is not working properly,

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:27.710
it can put a lot of strain on
different parts of the heart,

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:29.990
therefore making the
heart essentially function

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:32.020
at a much lower rate, which is deadly.

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:32.980
For this child,

00:05:32.980 --> 00:05:35.120
because his heart isn't
pumping blood effectively,

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:36.470
it's affecting his kidneys.

00:05:36.470 --> 00:05:38.120
His kidneys aren't getting enough blood

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:39.730
and therefore are slowly failing.

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:41.550
One of the most important factors

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:43.690
in deciding whether or
not to operate on somebody

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:47.470
is their chance of having
side effects from surgery,

00:05:47.470 --> 00:05:48.920
which means decreased blood flow,

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:51.620
possible chance of
infection, renal failure.

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:54.520
Doogie Howser's right in this
case, at least in my mind.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:56.080
The child's a very high-risk patient

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:57.920
and it's better to repair the valve first

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:00.400
and then go ahead with the
possible heart transplant

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:01.233
later on.

